AWS Signature Version 4 test vectors for the S3 object store (tools/internal/live/objectstore.go,
TestS3SigV4Vectors). Fetched once on 2026-10-08; the tests read only these files, never the network.

aws4_testsuite/
  The published AWS SigV4 test suite as botocore vendors it, copied byte for byte from
  boto/botocore commit bfb412faf00c249a54816e287a09a8bb79442c65,
  tests/unit/auth/aws4_testsuite/<name>/<name>.{req,creq,sts,authz} (Apache License 2.0).
  Signing inputs, from that commit's tests/unit/auth/test_sigv4.py: access key AKIDEXAMPLE, secret
  wJalrXUtnFEMI/K7MDENG+bPxRfiCYEXAMPLEKEY, region us-east-1, service "service", time
  2015-08-30T12:36:00Z.
  Kept: the GET vectors without path normalisation (S3 does not normalise paths) and without a
  session token. Left out: post-*, normalize-path/*, post-sts-token/*, get-space and the other
  non-GET vectors; nothing here signs a POST, a token or a dot-segment path.

s3-examples/
  The four worked examples of Amazon S3 API Reference, "Signature Calculations for the
  Authorization Header: Transferring Payload in a Single Chunk (AWS Signature Version 4)"
  (sig-v4-header-based-auth.html; read from the docs.aws.eu mirror,
  /AmazonS3/latest/developerguide/sig-v4-header-based-auth.html, on 2026-10-08), transcribed into
  the suite's file layout: Example: GET Object, PUT Object, GET Bucket Lifecycle, Get Bucket (List
  Objects). Signing inputs from the same page: access key AKIAIOSFODNN7EXAMPLE, secret
  wJalrXUtnFEMI/K7MDENG/bPxRfiCYEXAMPLEKEY, region us-east-1, service s3, time 2013-05-24T00:00:00Z.
  Transcription choices: header lines written as `Name:value` without the page's trailing spaces
  (canonicalisation trims them anyway); the PUT example's request line `PUT test$file.text` is
  written `PUT /test$file.text` (the canonical request on the same page has `/test%24file.text`);
  its body is the page's "Welcome to Amazon S3." whose SHA-256 is the page's x-amz-content-sha256;
  the bucket-level examples' `GET ?lifecycle` / `GET ?max-keys=2&prefix=J` are written with the
  path `/`; the Authorization values keep the page's `,` separators (the suite uses `, `).
